<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Offensive CAP Belarus, 2015</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P class=yiv0838570415MsoNormal&gt;&lt;B id=yui_3_16_0_1_1430183454574_2777&gt;&lt;SPAN id=yui_3_16_0_1_1430183454574_2776 style="FONT-SIZE: 9pt"&gt;&lt;IMG alt=http://www.raf.mod.uk/rafcms/mediafiles/6D372B73_5056_A318_A8CB37319C1DB992.jpg src="http://www.raf.mod.uk/rafcms/mediafiles/6D372B73_5056_A318_A8CB37319C1DB992.jpg"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=yiv0838570415MsoNormal&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 9pt"&gt;09 April 2015&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN id=yui_3_16_0_1_1430183454574_2758 style="FONT-SIZE: 9pt"&gt;&lt;BR clear=none&gt;&lt;BR clear=none&gt;Backed by Russia, Belarus has invaded Poland’s eastern provinces in force.&amp;nbsp; Armored units with heavy artillery and infantry support crossed the border before dawn yesterday and appear to be driving on Bialystok and Lublin.&amp;nbsp; Airmobile units, possibly Russian, have taken several bridge crossings.&amp;nbsp; While the assault was expected Polish and NATO intelligence did not anticipate it for another 4-6 days.&amp;nbsp; Polish forces have given ground but they are expected to be able to hold the line while NATO brings sufficient air and ground forces to bear to eliminate the incursion.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P id=yui_3_16_0_1_1430183454574_2759 class=yiv0838570415MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 9pt"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P id=yui_3_16_0_1_1430183454574_2760 class=yiv0838570415MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN id=yui_3_16_0_1_1430183454574_2761 style="FONT-SIZE: 9pt"&gt;It is expected that further Russian forces will be brought into action when the Belarus Army’s offensive stalls.&amp;nbsp; The USAF 555&lt;SUP&gt;th&lt;/SUP&gt; Fighter Squadron (555 FS, 24 F-16C) and the Polish 40&lt;SUP&gt;th&lt;/SUP&gt; Tactical Squadron (40.ELT, 24 Su-22M4) have been tasked to strike key logistic and support sites in Belarus to complicate enemy reinforcement efforts.&amp;nbsp; They will be supported by a NATO E-3 Sentry and four EA-18Gs from the US Navy’s VAQ-139.&amp;nbsp; Your task is to provide air cover for the operation using the 18 Typhoon FGR.4s of 1 Sqdn RAF.&amp;nbsp; Enemy air activity is expected to be heavy; ground defenses are not a factor.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P id=yui_3_16_0_1_1430183454574_2775 class=yiv0838570415MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 9pt"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P id=yui_3_16_0_1_1430183454574_2762 class=yiv0838570415MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 9pt"&gt;Units:&amp;nbsp; ~130 total; 18 aircraft in player control&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 9pt"&gt;Scenario Time:&amp;nbsp; 3 hours&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P id=yui_3_16_0_1_1430183454574_2764 class=yiv0838570415MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 9pt"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P id=yui_3_16_0_1_1430183454574_2765 class=yiv0838570415MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN id=yui_3_16_0_1_1430183454574_2774 style="FONT-SIZE: 9pt"&gt;Designers Note:&amp;nbsp; This scenario started as a way to test the effectiveness of various fighters using an offensive fighter sweep mission; hence the lack of ground defenses.&amp;nbsp; I built the targets, the strikes, and the defenders and realized I had about 90% of a releasable scenario… why not put it out there?&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
